window.docContents[160].resolve({"/Indistinguishable-function/#Consistency-of-global-optimization-algorithms--Indistinguishable-function--Lipschitz-property":{"contents":"We show that \\tilde{f} is Lipschitz continuous. Writing \\tilde{f} = f + g on B(c, \\varepsilon / 2) and \\tilde{f} = f elsewhere, the Lipschitz function g is nonnegative inside the ball and nonpositive outside of it. Hence \\tilde{f} = f + \\max(g, 0), which is Lipschitz as a sum of Lipschitz functions (see LipschitzWith.if). This argument only uses the metric structure of \\alpha: no vector space structure is required.\n\n\n\n","context":"Consistency of global optimization algorithms\u0009Indistinguishable function","header":"4.2. Lipschitz property","id":"/Indistinguishable-function/#Consistency-of-global-optimization-algorithms--Indistinguishable-function--Lipschitz-property"}});